els weird to me. Blocking third-party cookies isn't really a RWS-related preference, so the `SetPrivacySandboxRelatedWebsiteSetsPreferences` name doesn't really fit IMO. WDYT about just…"],["efdadcec_e4983882",42,-7,1,"Similar to the other comment - it seems like it'd be simpler to just inline the call to SetBoolean in the one place it's needed, rather than adding a helper function that's only used once."],["f78e9bb9_1ab553d6",40,-7,1,"Personal preference: this is only called in one place, so it feels like it would be simpler to just inline the call to SetBoolean, instead of pulling it out into this helper."],["241f1a8c_e7927d7a",41,-6,1,"Typo"],["40273c4b_695e08e6",41,-6,1,"It looks like many tests need this line. Would it be simpler to just add this to the base class's `SetUp`, instead of requiring each individual test to call it? I don't think any of the tests rely on…"],["41de5d6f_1f2f16f9",41,-6,1,"Please don't move the declaration of `ukm_recorder`, since IIUC that isn't necessary for this CL and just pollutes the git blame. Same comment elsewhere."],["6f9ed368_dba528d2",40,-6,0,"IMO, we don't need to justify why we're enabling RWS, since this is an RWS-focused test. The fact that RWS is now deprecated should be irrelevant to this test (as you know, since you're writing this…"],["80e67cd1_4846db87",43,-6,1,"It's not helpful for the reader to know what *used* to set the preference (but doesn't anymore), and IMO it would be helpful to know more about what \"recreate preference state\" means, specifically.…"],["a8c4e7bc_d521b23f",40,-6,1,"This comment sort of implies that cookies within a RWS aren't blocked. That's not technically true, but either way, I think it's irrelevant since this test has nothing to do with cookies.…"],["c9abfba9_67214afd",43,-6,1,"Typo"],["d4adca72_d749b0e1",44,-6,1,"I don't see any uses of this name, is this forward-declaration actually used?"]],0,78],[7232010,20430,27,1.035,0.792,[[5,0.733,5,20],[49,0.267,0,7]],[],0,79],[7156563,20430,2